{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"agent_message","text":"The plan shape will be two executable goals: one for creating the button-chain behavior in `button-chain.html`, and one for completion styling plus browser-story verification. I’m adding one work unit per concrete target and one separate verification unit for the UI story, so execution cannot hide implementation and proof inside a broad step."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'PLANNING_SKILL_DIR=/tmp/ai-skills-capsules/20260811T200821Z-clean-current-iterative/current/worker/planning\nPLAN_DIR=basic-test-proof-current-20260811T200821Z-clean-current-iterative-isolated-plan\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" current-state '\"\\\\\n  -p 2.1: \\\"This benchmark workspace contains benchmark-test.md, task-spec.md, worker-prompt.md, session-id.txt, and the tagged repository-local planning skill capsule. No HTML has been created, opened, served, inspected, or tested during this proof.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 2.2: \\\"The future implementation target is a new repository-root file named button-chain.html; current source discovery is intentionally limited to the benchmark task specification and the tagged planning skill.\\\" \n\\\"\"'$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" desired-outcome '\"\\\\\n  -p 3.1: \\\"A future executor can create button-chain.html with one initial button, append exactly one button below the current last button when that current last button is pressed, and clear the document when the fourth generated button is pressed.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 3.2: \\\"The terminal completion state prints the exact lowercase text finished and displays it with a visible white border.\\\" \n\\\"\"'$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" approach '\"\\\\\n  -p 4.1: \\\"Create the document structure first, add atomic click handling for the current-last-button rule, add the fourth-generated-button completion branch, then add the completion border styling and future verification.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 4.2: \\\"Keep markup, behavior, style, automated test design, and browser-story validation as separate work units so reviewers can approve each target independently.\\\" \n\\\"\"'$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" scope '\"\\\\\n  -p 5.1: \\\"In scope: planning the creation of button-chain.html, its button append behavior, its fourth-generated-button completion behavior, its finished text styling, and future verification evidence.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 5.2: \\\"Out of scope for this planning-only proof: creating or editing HTML, opening or inspecting HTML, serving files, starting a browser, starting a server, running a driver, or executing UI tests.\\\" \n\\\"\"'$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" affected-areas '\"\\\\\n  -p 6.1: \\\"Future affected file: button-chain.html. Planned DOM scope: #button-chain-root. Planned behavior scopes: appendNextButton and finishOnFourthGeneratedButton. Planned style scope: .finished-message.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 6.2: \\\"No backend services, package managers, database state, browser runtime, or external systems are part of this proof.\\\" \n\\\"\"'$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" constraints-and-decisions '\"\\\\\n  -p 7.1: \\\"The benchmark requires using only the tagged repository-local planning skill and task files. The exact benchmark plan directory contains uppercase timestamp characters, so create-plan.sh was run against a temporary kebab-case directory and the helper-generated scaffold was moved to the required path.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 7.2: \\\"The future implementation must preserve the exact lowercase completion text finished and must make the white border visible; no hidden seed IDs, mutation labels, or unlisted task changes are part of the plan.\\\" \n\\\"\"'$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" risks-and-open-questions '\"\\\\\n  -p 8.1: \\\"Risk: a future executor could miscount the initial button as generated; the plan defines generated buttons as only buttons appended after user clicks.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 8.2: \\\"Open question for future implementation only: exact button labels are unspecified, so the plan assumes accessible labels that expose sequence numbers without changing the required completion text.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/create-ui-validation.sh\" \"$PLAN_DIR\" \"Future local browser opening of button-chain.html; not executed during this planning-only proof\"\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/add-goal.sh\" \"$PLAN_DIR\" 01-button-chain-behavior \"Create button chain behavior\" \"button-chain.html can be created with the initial button, current-last-button append rule, fourth-generated-button clearing rule, and an automated behavior test design.\"\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/add-goal.sh\" \"$PLAN_DIR\" 02-completion-and-ui-proof \"Verify completion presentation\" \"The completion presentation has a visible white border and the future browser story proves the complete click chain through direct user interaction.\"\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --testing-requirement \"$PLAN_DIR\" 01-button-chain-behavior yes \"This goal defines observable DOM behavior and owns an automated test-design work unit.\"\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --testing-requirement \"$PLAN_DIR\" 02-completion-and-ui-proof yes \"This goal defines visible presentation and owns the browser-story verification work unit.\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
