{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'PLANNING_SKILL_DIR=/tmp/ai-skills-capsules/20260811T200821Z-clean-current-iterative/current/worker/planning\nPLAN_DIR=basic-test-proof-current-20260811T200821Z-clean-current-iterative-isolated-plan\n# Goal 01 narrative\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" 01-button-chain-behavior current-state -p 2.1: \"No implementation file exists in this proof. Future execution begins by creating button-chain.html from the task contract only.\"\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" 01-button-chain-behavior why-needed -p 4.1: \"This goal owns the core behavior: the initial button, the exact append rule, the fourth-generated completion branch, and behavior-level test design.\"\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" 01-button-chain-behavior scope -p 5.1: \"In scope: one HTML file, one initial button, generated-button counting, last-button-only clicks, completion text, and automated behavior checks. Out of scope: CSS border styling and browser-story execution, which are owned by goal 02.\"\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" 01-button-chain-behavior affected-areas -p 6.1: \"button-chain.html scopes #button-chain-root, appendNextButton, finishOnFourthGeneratedButton, and buttonChainBehaviorTest.\"\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" 01-button-chain-behavior dependencies -p 7.1: \"No prior goal is required. This goal hands W03 completion state and W04 behavior proof design to goal 02.\"\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" 01-button-chain-behavior implementation -p 8.1: \"Track generated buttons separately from the initial button so the fourth generated button is the fourth appended button. The click handler must reject clicks on any button that is not currently last.\"\n# Goal 02 narrative\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" 02-completion-and-ui-proof current-state -p 2.1: \"Goal 02 depends on goal 01 defining the finished terminal state and behavior proof design. Browser execution is future work and is not run in this benchmark.\"\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" 02-completion-and-ui-proof why-needed -p 4.1: \"The user-visible completion requirement includes presentation, not only behavior, so it needs a separate style target and a direct-interaction UI story.\"\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" 02-completion-and-ui-proof scope -p 5.1: \"In scope: .finished-message white border styling and the US-01 browser story. Out of scope: changing the behavior contract already owned by goal 01.\"\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" 02-completion-and-ui-proof affected-areas -p 6.1: \"button-chain.html scope .finished-message and verification flow US-01.\"\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" 02-completion-and-ui-proof dependencies -p 7.1: \"Requires W01 through W03 before styling can be meaningfully attached and requires W05 before W06 can pass. Handoff is a validated future UI story with no open UI bugs.\"\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" 02-completion-and-ui-proof implementation -p 8.1: \"Use a visible white border on the completion element and verify it through rendered UI evidence after direct clicks, not by console state inspection.\"\n# Steps content concise\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" 01-button-chain-behavior/01-step-initial-markup instructions -p 5.1: \"Create button-chain.html with a valid HTML document, a #button-chain-root subtree, and exactly one initial button visible in the starting state.\"\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" 01-button-chain-behavior/01-step-initial-markup acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"A reviewer can identify one initial button and no pre-generated buttons in the initial document structure.\"\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" 01-button-chain-behavior/01-step-initial-markup handoff -p 7.1: \"W02 can attach behavior to the initial button and the future generated-button container.\"\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" 01-button-chain-behavior/02-step-append-handler instructions -p 5.1: \"Implement appendNextButton so a click on the current last button appends exactly one new button below it and updates last-button ownership to the appended button.\"\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" 01-button-chain-behavior/02-step-append-handler acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"Each accepted current-last click increases the button count by one; clicking an older button after a new button exists appends nothing.\"\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" 01-button-chain-behavior/02-step-append-handler handoff -p 7.1: \"W03 can consume the generated-button count and last-button state.\"\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" 01-button-chain-behavior/03-step-fourth-generated-finish instructions -p 5.1: \"Implement finishOnFourthGeneratedButton so pressing the fourth appended button clears the existing document content and renders only the completion state text finished.\"\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-section \"$PLAN_DIR\" 01-button-chain-behavior/03-step-fourth-generated-finish acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"The fourth generated button triggers a cleared document 